The `combineCorners` branch of `gsBoxTopology::allComponents` is broken in two ways.

```cpp
else
{
    component_coll_t last;
    for( typename map_t::iterator it = comps[i].begin(); it != comps[i].end(); ++it )
    {
        const index_t nrcp = it->second.size();
        for (index_t j=0; j<nrcp; ++j)
            last.push_back(it->second[i]);   // uses i, not j
    }
}                                            // last is never added to result
```

1. **Wrong loop index.** The inner loop runs over `j` but reads `it->second[i]`. This branch only runs when `i == 0`, so it pushes `it->second[0]` `nrcp` times. The other patch corners for each vertex are never collected, and the entry is duplicated instead.

2. **The combined corner group is discarded.** `last` is a local that goes out of scope without `result.push_back(last)`. With `combineCorners == true`, the returned decomposition has no corner component at all.

**Why it matters.** The new `setupSubspaceCorrectedMassSmoother` in `multiGrid_example.cpp` calls `mb.topology().allComponents(true)`. It then builds the additive smoother from those components. Because the corner group is missing:
- The corner DoFs get no transfer matrix and no local solver.
- The additive operator has a null space on the corner DoFs.
- The resulting smoother/preconditioner is singular there, so multigrid on multi-patch domains will not reduce error components at the vertices.

**Secondary point.** `sz` is computed as the sum of all map sizes and used for `reserve`. That count does not match what the function claims to return when corners are combined. This is harmless, but it shows the branch was not exercised.

